/*  EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.
    A method stores its argument in the object it is cast on. Cast inside a rabbit, with the argument made there and the object outside.

    The object a method is cast on is a parameter like any other. (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O4). */

Define object bag with (the series of series of number items).
Bind void to keep unto bag, given (the series of number s):
    Insert s into one's items.
Done.
Define b as a new bag { the items (a series of series of number) }.
Pull a rabbit.
    Define inner as a series of number with (1, 2, 3).
    Cast keep on (b, inner).
Done.
State b's items.
